{{!
    @template assignsubmission_vrtour/form_card

    The tour on the submission form: what a tour is, what this one still needs, and the way into the editor.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * started - whether the tour has a photo
    * items - the checklist (see assignsubmission_vrtour/checklist)
    * editurl, editlabel - the editor link, when the user may edit
    * note - the unsaved-fields note, when the form has other parts
    * owneronly - the note shown to anyone else
    * hidesave - 1 when the form's own Save button has nothing to add (drafts, no other submission type)

    Example context (json):
    {"started": false, "items": [{"done": false, "label": "At least one 360° photo", "count": "0 so far"}],
     "editurl": "#", "editlabel": "Build your tour", "note": "", "owneronly": "", "hidesave": 1}
}}
<div class="card assignsubmission_vrtour-card" data-region="assignsubmission_vrtour-card" data-hidesave="{{hidesave}}">
    <div class="card-body d-flex flex-wrap gap-3 align-items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0">{{> assignsubmission_vrtour/illustration }}</div>
        <div class="flex-grow-1" style="min-width: 14rem">
            {{^started}}<p class="mb-2">{{#str}}tourwhat, assignsubmission_vrtour{{/str}}</p>{{/started}}
            <p class="fw-bold mb-1">{{#str}}checklistheading, assignsubmission_vrtour{{/str}}</p>
            {{> assignsubmission_vrtour/checklist }}
            {{#editurl}}
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg mt-3" href="{{editurl}}" data-region="assignsubmission_vrtour-edit">{{editlabel}}</a>
            {{/editurl}}
            {{#note}}<p class="form-text text-body-secondary mb-0 mt-2">{{note}}</p>{{/note}}
            {{#owneronly}}<p class="text-body-secondary mb-0 mt-2">{{owneronly}}</p>{{/owneronly}}
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
